    <string name="help_section_calendar_views">Calendar Views</string>
    <string name="help_calendar_views_1">The application has two main views: Monthly and Yearly. You can switch between them from the side menu (3 lines).</string>
    <string name="help_calendar_views_2">In the monthly view, swipe left or right to change the month. The upper left arrow in the header will return to the current month.</string>
    <string name="help_section_event_management">Event Management</string>
    <string name="help_event_management_1">Tap on a day in the monthly calendar to see its events or add a new one. Events can also be created by tapping on the (+) icon in the header.</string>
    <string name="help_event_management_2">Events (single or repeated) can be edited and deleted in any calendar that is editable.</string>
    <string name="help_section_event_list">Event List</string>
    <string name="help_event_list_1">Below the monthly calendar, the list of events for the month is displayed. In the current month, you can toggle between seeing only Pending events or the full list of All by pressing the central arrow button located in the list header. Each event can be edited and deleted by clicking on it.</string>
    <string name="help_section_customization">Customization</string>
    <string name="help_customization_1">From the side menu you can manage your calendars and data maintenance. In Settings you can choose Light/Dark mode and customize the interface colors.</string>
    <string name="help_section_holiday_manager">Holiday Manager</string>
    <string name="help_holiday_manager_1">This feature allows you to manually mark specific days as holidays or working days, regardless of what the system calendar or imported events indicate. When marking a day as a holiday, its number will be highlighted in the corresponding color in the monthly and yearly views.</string>
    <string name="help_section_widget">Widget</string>
    <string name="help_widget_1">The application includes a Widget for the Home screen that shows upcoming events. You can customize its appearance by choosing the number of events to show, changing the font size and modifying its colors.</string>
